    "structure": "CSharp uses per-function/main named candidates plus declaration order and restores nested function state. SLG uses exact global lexical symbols, type facts, canonical child/flow-source indexes and declaration-owned returns before lowering. Both preserve known length/unknown/growable-required state.",
    "branches": "Dynamic literals/typed empty register; direct push adds one; control-dependent push or other mutation makes length unknown; mutable formal calls make length unknown. Reserve/capacity and owning append/updated require growable storage. Zero/unknown/required suppress S003. Declared calls retain precedence over intrinsic spellings. Block primary source has no callee-supplied requirement; additional ordinary arguments retain expected type.",
    "logic": "CSharp marks name candidates from reference-unwrapped dynamic/bounded expected types at field construction, explicit/implicit returns, formal/generic/enum arguments, pushed dynamic owners and indexed assignment. SLG consumes current resolved ordinary/interpolation call arguments, enum payload arguments, nominal field expected IDs, indexed assignment value IDs and genuine function-owned declared returns. Synthetic input/self declarations cannot replace return owner. Current lexical binding type facts precede collection and path inference preserves the immediate receiver.",
    "diagnostics": "Both warn only for a known positive length with no required growable storage. CSharp emits declaration location; SLG derives the same binding-name token, mutable suffix and module, then merges warning order by line/column/code. The complete original29 retains exact stdout/stderr and additional-source order. No case or oracle changed."
